Kiali native-port material:
The health primitives/calculator, host resolution, Sidecar import/export scope,
root-selector and egress checks, namespace-aware Service registry,
VirtualService destination checks, host-conflict grouping and outbound-policy defaults,
PeerAuthentication pattern checks and resolved mesh-root behavior,
selectorless PeerAuthentication namespace grouping,
DestinationRule peer-policy checks and namespace/root filtering,
Gateway API class registry and membership checks,
Gateway API listener/address collision checks and validation merging,
Istio Gateway selector/port/hostname conflict checks and wildcard settings,
configured mTLS composition,
application-label behavior, Gateway route checks, AuthorizationPolicy pattern
and host-registry checks with namespace export filtering,
WorkloadGroup-to-WorkloadEntry label-selector relationships,
WorkloadGroup application-label selection and VM correlation provenance,
Pod-attributed service-account observations without principal or permission inference,
WorkloadEntry probe-condition interpretation with explicit disabled-check assumptions,
validation-exclusion parsing, ServiceEntry/DestinationRule conflict grouping,
proxy summaries and observed-name Service/configuration-candidate lookup,
traffic graph identities/projections and namespace-name membership, traffic histogram query construction,
counter metric definitions and rate-query construction,
custom aggregate dashboard raw/rate/classic-histogram query shapes and unit-scale defaults,
Service traffic-generation shapes/defaults,
TCP traffic-shifting wizard generation,
circuit-breaker wizard capabilities,
load-balancing and affinity wizard capabilities,
HTTP mirroring wizard shapes and shadow-only forwarding behavior,
outbound TLS mode and file-reference wizard capabilities,
inbound PeerAuthentication mTLS wizard mode controls,
Gateway HTTP/gRPC backend traffic-weight controls,
HTTP timeout/retry/fault creation shapes,
HTTP request-route ordering behavior,
HTTP request-condition fields and AND/OR grouping,
granular HTTP condition preservation and empty-alternative guards,
tracing HTTP models, correlation references and
generated parity evidence derive from Kiali v2.33.0,
commit 0e8be887b8217bbcac5e3ae0bfcd258073949cca, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/kiali/kiali
Detailed source identities and reproduction instructions: test-files/README.md.

Tempo query interoperability:
Typed span/resource/event/link/instrumentation attribute, literal-name and
span/trace-intrinsic query construction follows the public TraceQL HTTP/language
contract. Parser and operator behavior was inspected at Tempo commit
afbbb308bbad6caa74fe33f4f122aff6275974f8. No Tempo server code is bundled.
Documentation: https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/latest/traceql/construct-traceql-queries/

Istio example manifests:
Bookinfo and example Prometheus manifests are reproduced from Istio 1.30.6,
commit b85dac9587f2f997151d205e069e4f4ff091c7c5, under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/istio/istio
Their original content is preserved; development overlays are separate files.

Istio resource models:
The schema-derived TypeScript models are generated from sanitized Istio CRD
spec/status schemas captured from the managed asm-1-30 verification environment.
The source schema snapshot and SHA-256 provenance are in
test-files/configuration/schemas.json and the generated source headers.

Gateway API and inference-extension resource models:
Schema-derived types include Apache-2.0 material from kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api
v1.6.0 (89b3b0c3fa63f9342f43ba0fb2cf93d6aab53af7) and
kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api-inference-extension v1.5.0
(df9f8909fe06fe2dfd4a6fc0bd0c01a0acabf849).
Per-file Git blob identities are recorded in
test-files/configuration/gateway-schemas.json.

